      "writtenOn": "2022-11-24T10:47:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "__be16 is purely a type annotation that helps with code readability (ie. it documents intent).\n\nIn practice it is simply a u16 / uint16 (ie. unsigned short).\nie. the compiler doesn\u0027t do anything special (unfortunately...)\n\nSo storing x0403 into it will - again byte swap - because of little endianness of our cpu.  So ultimately on the wire it ends up being 03 04.\n\nNote that here ip_id is a variable and effectively endianness less,\nthe real write is when we store ip_id into struct iphdr ip.id in line 155 below.",
